hip-bundle-arch: a fix to intel/llvm v7.1.1, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

A kernel bundle (get_kernel_bundle) of a program built for several AMD architectures got the first one's image:
AMD images carry no compile_target, the runtime asked the HIP adapter about each image alone without handing it
the image, and the adapter takes the first AMD image as a fallback when it finds no exact match.  The GPU then
refused it (hipErrorInvalidImage), so an engine with code for every AMD GPU a package covers found no usable GPU.
A kernel submitted to a queue was not affected: that path hands the adapter every image and their bytes.  Fixed,
the runtime hands the HIP adapter the image too, as it does the CUDA one, and the adapter does not fall back on a
clang offload bundle that lacks the device's architecture.
---
diff --git a/sycl/source/detail/program_manager/program_manager.cpp b/sycl/source/detail/program_manager/program_manager.cpp
--- a/sycl/source/detail/program_manager/program_manager.cpp
+++ b/sycl/source/detail/program_manager/program_manager.cpp
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 // Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the CUDA adapter is handed the device image itself (cuda-binary-to-adapter)
 // Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the CUDA adapter is handed every NVIDIA image (cuda-binaries-to-adapter)
 // Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: NVIDIA images in a fatbin selected by architecture (cuda-binaries-to-adapter-2)
+// Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the HIP adapter is handed the device image too (hip-bundle-arch)
 //
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
@@ -556,6 +557,12 @@
       DevBin.BinaryStart, std::distance(DevBin.BinaryStart, DevBin.BinaryEnd)};
   if (DeviceImpl.getBackend() == backend::ext_oneapi_cuda)
     UrBinary.pNext = &Blob;
+  // and the HIP adapter refuses a bundle for another AMD architecture: AMD
+  // images carry no compile_target, so a kernel bundle (get_kernel_bundle),
+  // whose images this checks one at a time, got the first architecture's of a
+  // program built for several, which the GPU then refused
+  if (DeviceImpl.getBackend() == backend::ext_oneapi_hip)
+    UrBinary.pNext = &Blob;
 
   ur_result_t Error = Adapter.call_nocheck<UrApiKind::urDeviceSelectBinary>(
       URDeviceHandle, &UrBinary,
